oup\nL60: \nL61: the gun lobby\nL62: \nL63: the oil lobby\nL64: \nL65: lobby\nL66: \nL67: 2 of 2\nL68: ## 【19†verb】\nL69: \nL70: lobbied; lobbying\nL71: \nL72: 【20†intransitive verb】\nL73: \nL74: : to conduct activities aimed at influencing public officials and especially members of a legislative body on legislation\nL75: \nL76: 【21†transitive verb】\nL77: \nL78: 1\nL79: \nL80: : to promote (something, such as a project) or secure the passage of (legislation) by influencing public officials\nL81: \nL82: lobby a bill through Congress\nL83: \nL84: 2\nL85: \nL86: : to attempt to influence or sway (someone, such as a public official) toward a desired action\nL87: \nL88: lobbying senators for tax reform\nL89: \nL90: lobbyer noun\nL91: \nL92: lobbyism\nL93: 【22†ˈlä-bē-ˌi-zəm 】\nL94: \nL95: noun\nL96: ## Synonyms of lobby\nL97: \nL98: Relevance\nL99: \nL100: Noun\nL101: \nL102:   * 【23†foyer】\nL103:   * 【24†hall】\nL104: \nL105: 【17†See All Synonyms & Antonyms in Thesaurus】\nL106: ## Examples of lobby in a Sentence\nL107: \nL108: Noun I'll meet you in the lobby after the show. The proposed new law is supported by the oil lobby. Verb an organization that has been lobbying for reform of the tax laws The health-care industry has lobbied against the proposal. an organization that has been lobbying Congress for reform of the tax laws a player who has lobbied hard to be included in the team's starting lineup I lobbied our company for a new computer. See More\nL109: \nL110: Recent Examples on the Web\nL111: Examples are automatically compiled from online sources to show current usage. 【14†Read More】 Opinions expressed in the examples do not represent those of Merriam-Webster or its editors. 【25†Send us feedback†docs.google.com】.\nL112: \nL113: Noun\nL114: Inside, the lobby is dimly lit in soothing lavender and blue and house music is piped in by surround sound. — Condé Nast, Condé Nast Traveler, 8 Oct. 2026 One floor up from the lobby, on the floor of the exchange, Skydance CEO David Ellison, co-CEO Ynon Kreiz and the entire senior leadership team gathered to ring the opening bell. — Alex Weprin, HollywoodReporter, 8 Oct. 2026\nL115: \nL116: Verb\nL117: Trump has long lobbied to receive the award and continued to do so this week. — Christopher Tremoglie, The Washington Examiner, 9 Oct. 2026 Protesting contractors and lobbying local officials Other opponents are pressing local governments not to assist contractors. — Rebecca Santana, Los Angeles Times, 9 Oct. 2026 【26†See All Example Sentences for lobby】\nL118: ## Word History\nL119: \nL120: Etymology\nL121: \nL122: Noun\nL123: \nL124: Medieval Latin lobium gallery, of Germanic origin; akin to Old High German louba porch\nL125: \nL126: First Known Use\nL127: \nL128: Noun\nL129: \nL130: 1596, in the meaning defined at 【27†sense 1】\nL131: \nL132: Verb\nL133: \nL134: 1820, in the meaning defined at 【28†intransitive sense】\nL135: \nL136: Time Traveler\nL137: \nL138: The first known use of lobby was in 1596\nL139: \nL140: 【29†See more words from the same year】\nL141: \nL142: ## Browse Nearby Words\nL143: \nL144: 【30†lobber】\nL145: \nL146: lobby\nL147: \nL148: 【31†lobbyer】\nL149: \nL150: 【32†See all Nearby Words】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nADVOCACY Definition & Meaning - Merriam-Webster (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/advocacy)\nciteturn41view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/advocacy\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 182\nL0: 【0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】 【1†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com】\nL1: \nL2: [Input: Search Dictionary]\nL3: \nL4:   * 【2†Games】\nL5:   * 【3†Word of the Day】\nL6:   * 【4†Grammar】\nL7:   * 【5†Word Finder】\nL8:   * 【6†Slang】\nL9:   * 【7†Newsletters】\nL10:   * 【8†Wordplay】\nL11:   * 【9†Rhymes】\nL12:   * 【10†Thesaurus】\nL13:   * 【11†Join MWU†unabridged.merriam-webster.com】\nL14:   * More\nL15:     * 【2†Games】\nL1